 | Cloud-shadow distance fade, far-field rings, haze and low-sun colour (`GlslLib`, `CloudLayer`, `FarField.cs`, `G2TerrainEffects.FarField`, `SceneLighting.AerialTerms`) | none new (procedural; the far field's existing biome colours) | the shadow's depth faded with the camera distance; rings 7 % apart with wider normal footprints; normals flattened and the horizon's colour blended in with distance; a greener crop mean and a green floor with the sun low; the valley haze's phase and sun term reduced near the horizon | project code | own |
 | Sky streaks and heap edges (`GlslLib.CloudLib` domain, `PostEffects` sky pass) | none (procedural) | less stretch; gap and fray noise; two fine edge octaves; the unlit far side darker with the sun low; chroma held at 0.35 saturation | project code | own |
-| Prisoner placement, the fallen relaxed apart (`TraceCrowd.RelaxFallen`), four surrender poses, fallen arms laid down, tilted shields, a no-weapon crowd view (`TraceCrowd`, `CrowdPoseVariants.DeriveKneelArms`/`LayArmsDown`, `CrowdAnimationBank`, `CrowdRenderer`) | the crowd LOD meshes (§3.12) and the CMU-derived `kneel`, `death_fwd` and `death_back` clips (§3.4, §3.9); the battle trace (§3.13), read only | two more poses derived from the kneel by turning the arms and bowing the head; the death clips' arms laid down once the body is down; the fallen bodies pushed apart by Jacobi passes and lifted off the living (at most 2.5 m from the trace); per LOD mesh a view with the shield but not the weapon; offsets and tilts pure functions of the trace and entity ids | project code (the poses and laid-down clips are derivatives of CMU-derived clips: `LicenseRef-CMU-Mocap`, as the clips they are made from) | own / PROTOTYPE-ONLY (as the CMU base) |
+| Prisoner placement, the fallen relaxed apart (`TraceCrowd.RelaxFallen`), the fallen beat's framing (`BenchAftermathScene.FallenViewScore`), four surrender poses, fallen arms laid down, tilted shields, a no-weapon crowd view (`TraceCrowd`, `CrowdPoseVariants.DeriveKneelArms`/`LayArmsDown`, `CrowdAnimationBank`, `CrowdRenderer`) | the crowd LOD meshes (§3.12) and the CMU-derived `kneel`, `death_fwd` and `death_back` clips (§3.4, §3.9); the battle trace (§3.13), read only | two more poses derived from the kneel by turning the arms and bowing the head; the death clips' arms laid down once the body is down; the fallen bodies pushed apart by Jacobi passes and lifted off the living (at most 2.5 m from the trace); per LOD mesh a view with the shield but not the weapon; offsets and tilts pure functions of the trace and entity ids | project code (the poses and laid-down clips are derivatives of CMU-derived clips: `LicenseRef-CMU-Mocap`, as the clips they are made from) | own / PROTOTYPE-ONLY (as the CMU base) |
 | Skin shade and penumbra (`CharEffects`), crowd beards (`CrowdEffects`), bronze helmets (`Helmets.Paint`) | the chars bake (§3.9), the generated helmets (§3.11) | a warm shade tone and a five-tap shadow average on skin; a dark-brown floor for beards and hair above the shoulders; a warmer, more saturated and smoother bronze with fewer bright scratches | project code | own |
 | Wetness cap, puddle mask, grass transmission cap (`GlslLib.shadePbrFullSpec`, `G2TerrainEffects`, `GroundCover`) | the render1 and env bakes (§3.8, §3.10) | the wet shading scaled to the dry one's luminance where brighter; puddles only on level, low relief; the light through a card capped at 1.5 times its lit albedo; a darker base-to-tip gradient | project code | own |
 | Wall weathering, boulders, hearth smoke (`StructureRenderer`, `Rocks.cs`, `Settlements.IronAgeVillage` hearths, `SmokeSource.Hearth`, `BenchBase`) | the env bakes (§3.10) | rain streaks, moss and grime on walls; darker, mossier boulders; thin smoke columns from some roundhouse roofs | project code | own |
